-  When a Simplified Formats MIME type is requested, the **CONTRIBUTION envelope itself is still returned as canonical JSON** (`uid`, `versions[]` metadata, `audit`). Only the inner `versions[i].data` payload (`COMPOSITION`, `EHR_STATUS`, or `FOLDER`) is serialized in the chosen FLAT or STRUCTURED form. See [Simplified Formats](../simplified_formats.html) for the rules that apply to that inner payload.
+  When a Simplified Formats MIME type is requested, the **CONTRIBUTION envelope itself is still returned as canonical JSON** (`uid`, `versions[]` metadata, `audit`). Only an inner `versions[i].data` payload that is a `COMPOSITION` is serialized in the chosen FLAT or STRUCTURED form; an `EHR_STATUS` or `FOLDER` payload stays canonical JSON, because the Simplified Formats define no mapping for either. See [Simplified Formats](../simplified_formats.html) for the rules that apply to that inner payload.
